  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best multimodal configs (scvi_n200 + resnet50) achieve ~0.54 accuracy, while rna_only with pca_n2000 is 0.485 and image_only is only 0.208. However, we lack a direct rna_only baseline using scvi_n200, the best-performing RNA encoder. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the image modality is genuinely contributing to the multimodal performance or whether the gains come entirely from the scvi_n200 encoder. Question tested: config_011 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) provides a clean single-variable comparison against config_028 (multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat = 0.5362), isolating the marginal contribution of the image branch. Why best use of budget: This is a foundational question — if rna_only with scvi_n200 approaches 0.54, the image adds little and future effort should focus on RNA improvements (multiprofile, aggregation); if it lags significantly, the image is genuinely informative and we should invest in better image encoders (e.g., imagenet_vit_l). No other single experiment resolves this uncertainty as directly, and the answer will efficiently guide all subsequent experiments."
}

